## GNU libunistring

The libunistring library is covered by the GNU Lesser General Public License (LGPL):
=> https://www.gnu.org/software/libunistring/manual/libunistring.html#GNU-LGPL GNU LGPL

## zlib

zlib is a compression library by Jean-loup Gailly and Mark Adler. It is under the zlib license.
=> https://www.zlib.net/zlib_license.html ZLIB License

## PCRE2

PCRE2 is a regular expression library by Philip Hazel and contributors. It is under the BSD 3-clause license with an exception for binary distributions.
=> https://github.com/PCRE2Project/pcre2/blob/master/LICENCE.md  PCRE2 license

## GNU libiconv

On platforms where the C library does not provide character set conversion, GNU libiconv is used. It is covered by the GNU Lesser General Public License (LGPL).
=> https://www.gnu.org/software/libiconv/  GNU libiconv
